I successfully completed the “Pyramid of Pain” room on TryHackMe, gaining a strong understanding of how Indicators of Compromise (IOCs) are categorized based on the level of difficulty they impose on adversaries when detected and mitigated.

This module is a foundational cybersecurity concept in threat intelligence and SOC operations, helping security analysts prioritize detection strategies that maximize disruption to attacker activities.

## Overview

  The Pyramid of Pain model illustrates the relationship between different types of security indicators and the “cost” to attackers when those indicators are detected and blocked. Lower-level indicators are easy for attackers to change, while higher-level behavioral indicators significantly increase the effort required to continue an attack campaign.

