## Key Takeaways
     -Lower-level indicators (hashes, IPs, domains) are easy to replace and offer short-term detection value.
     -Higher-level indicators (tools and TTPs) provide stronger defensive value by forcing attackers to change their behavior.
     -Effective SOC operations should prioritize behavioral detection and threat hunting over static indicators alone.
     -Understanding attacker adaptability is key to building resilient cybersecurity defenses.

